Negative control for filter-optional-indicator.test.ts.

Hardcodes the "Optional" suppression in the button group itself, overriding
whatever the element declared — the renderer keeping a presentation rule to itself
instead of honouring the uischema's `optionalText`. The assertion that the very
same column draws the word again once the option is lifted goes red; every
assertion that the shipped bar draws it nowhere stays green, which is exactly the
half a hardcoded suppression would otherwise satisfy.

